                <pb facs="0851" n="1685" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1685"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/1082a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-24T10:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 24, 1918, 10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4714. For McFadden [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 149. Following is for Alfred Smith now due Paris on way to Spain: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Bunkering arrangement expires June 25 as agreed, and we would suggest
                            that if you recommend extending date, we stipulate we will license
                            bunkers freely only from United States Atlantic and Gulf ports, reasons
                            for this being that we might desire to control boats going from Cuba to
                            Mexico or passing through the Canal. We would like your opinion promptly
                            as there is shortly due at the Panama Canal the Spanish boat <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Aviles</hi> with cargo of nitrate for Spain.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
